{"step_index":267,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:31:07Z","input_tokens":2829,"cache_read_tokens":100021,"output_tokens":343,"thinking":"The current path construction in `train.py` is not robust to execution context; the data path relies on the current working directory, which can vary. To fix this, the project root needs to be determined dynamically using `pathlib.Path` and then the data path constructed relative to the project root. This ensures the script can find the dataset regardless of where it's executed. Specifically, `PROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]` will be used to resolve the project root and then `DATA_PATH` will be constructed accordingly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\backend\\app\\ml\\train.py","Replacement":"from pathlib import Path\n\nPROJECT_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nDEFAULT_DATA_PATH = str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"data\" / \"synthetic_transactions.csv\")\nDEFAULT_MODEL_DIR = str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"model_store\")\n\ndef train_and_evaluate_pipeline(\n    data_path: str = DEFAULT_DATA_PATH,\n    model_dir: str = DEFAULT_MODEL_DIR\n):","Target":"def train_and_evaluate_pipeline(\n    data_path: str = \"data/synthetic_transactions.csv\",\n    model_dir: str = \"model_store\"\n):"}}]}
