{"step_index":275,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:32:53Z","input_tokens":2692,"cache_read_tokens":102403,"output_tokens":300,"thinking":"The data loading and splitting appear standard, with a reasonable fraud rate observed. Threshold tuning on the validation set resulted in the optimal configuration. The champion model, using HistGradientBoosting, demonstrates excellent performance on the held-out test set, far surpassing the baseline LogisticRegression model in precision and F1-score.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"Get-ChildItem \"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\model_store\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Check model_store artifacts"}}]}
{"step_index":276,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:32:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T19:02:58+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T19:02:59+05:30\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n\r\n\r\n    Directory: C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\model_store\r\n\r\n\r\nMode                 LastWriteTime         Length Name                                                                 \r\n----                 -------------         ------ ----                                                                 \r\n-a----        29-10-2026     19:02            820 evaluation_metrics.json                                              \r\n-a----        29-10-2026     19:02         171548 fraudlens_predictor.joblib                                           \r\n-a----        29-10-2026     19:02           1488 model_meta.json                                                      \r\n\r\n\r\n"}
{"step_index":277,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:32:59Z","input_tokens":2566,"cache_read_tokens":103068,"output_tokens":2452,"thinking":"Considering the graph analysis engine, the focus is on utilizing a graph library for analyzing relationships within the data, specifically focusing on connected components, shared entities, and relevant metrics. The goal is to generate an interactive graph that visualizes connections between transactions, accounts, merchants, devices, and IP addresses, dependent on the data's availability. This interactive graph should highlight specific patterns like shared devices, reused IP addresses, and rapid transaction bursts.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\"\"\nFraudLens AI - NetworkX Graph Relationship & Entity Clustering Engine\nConstructs multi-entity risk graphs connecting:\n- Transactions\n- User Accounts\n- Devices\n- IP Addresses\n- Merchants\n\nPerforms:\n- Bipartite entity projection (Account-Device-Account)\n- Connected components (fraud ring / syndicate detection)\n- Neighborhood ego-graph extraction for individual transactions\n- Edge justification (documenting why each relationship exists)\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\nimport networkx as nx\nimport pandas as pd\n\nclass FraudGraphEngine:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.graph = nx.Graph()\n        self.transaction_map = {}\n\n    def build_graph_from_dataframe(self, df: pd.DataFrame):\n        \"\"\"\n        Builds the global multi-entity graph from transaction records.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.graph.clear()\n        self.transaction_map.clear()\n\n        for _, row in df.iterrows():\n            txn_id = str(row[\"transaction_id\"])\n            account_id = str(row[\"account_id\"])\n            device_id = str(row.get(\"device_id\", \"DEV-UNKNOWN\"))\n            ip_addr = str(row.get(\"ip_address\", \"0.0.0.0\"))\n            merchant_id = str(row.get(\"merchant_id\", \"MER-UNKNOWN\"))\n            amount = float(row.get(\"amount\", 0.0))\n            is_fraud = int(row.get(\"is_fraud\", 0))\n            cat = str(row.get(\"merchant_category\", \"general\"))\n            timestamp = str(row.get(\"timestamp\", \"\"))\n\n            self.transaction_map[txn_id] = row.to_dict()\n\n            # 1. Add Transaction Node\n            self.graph.add_node(\n                txn_id,\n                node_type=\"transaction\",\n                label=f\"Txn {txn_id[-8:]}\",\n                amount=amount,\n                is_fraud=is_fraud,\n                timestamp=timestamp\n            )\n\n            # 2. Add Account Node\n            if not self.graph.has_node(account_id):\n                self.graph.add_node(\n                    account_id,\n                    node_type=\"account\",\n                    label=f\"Acc {account_id[-6:]}\",\n                    tx_count=0,\n                    total_volume=0.0\n                )\n            self.graph.nodes[account_id][\"tx_count\"] += 1\n            self.graph.nodes[account_id][\"total_volume\"] += amount\n\n            # 3. Add Device Node\n            if not self.graph.has_node(device_id):\n                self.graph.add_node(\n                    device_id,\n                    node_type=\"device\",\n                    label=f\"Dev {device_id[-6:]}\",\n                    accounts=set()\n                )\n            self.graph.nodes[device_id][\"accounts\"].add(account_id)\n\n            # 4. Add IP Node\n            if not self.graph.has_node(ip_addr):\n                self.graph.add_node(\n                    ip_addr,\n                    node_type=\"ip\",\n                    label=f\"IP {ip_addr}\",\n                    accounts=set()\n                )\n            self.graph.nodes[ip_addr][\"accounts\"].add(account_id)\n\n            # 5. Add Merchant Node\n            if not self.graph.has_node(merchant_id):\n                self.graph.add_node(\n                    merchant_id,\n                    node_type=\"merchant\",\n                    label=f\"Mer {merchant_id[-6:]}\",\n                    category=cat\n                )\n\n            # Connect Edges with Evidence Justification\n            self.graph.add_edge(\n                txn_id, account_id,\n                relation=\"ORIGINATED_FROM\",\n                evidence=\"Primary account holder initiated payment instruction.\"\n            )\n            self.graph.add_edge(\n                txn_id, device_id,\n                relation=\"CAPTURED_DEVICE\",\n                evidence=\"Device browser/hardware fingerprint captured at checkout.\"\n            )\n            self.graph.add_edge(\n                txn_id, ip_addr,\n                relation=\"ROUTED_THROUGH_IP\",\n                evidence=\"HTTP TCP/IP network connection packet header.\"\n            )\n            self.graph.add_edge(\n                txn_id, merchant_id,\n                relation=\"SETTLED_AT\",\n                evidence=\"Acquiring merchant terminal ID.\"\n            )\n\n    def get_ego_graph(self, txn_id: str, depth: int = 2) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Extracts the localized subnetwork around a specific transaction,\n        revealing shared devices, shared IPs, and correlated accounts.\n        \"\"\"\n        if txn_id not in self.graph:\n            return {\"nodes\": [], \"edges\": [], \"syndicate_cluster_size\": 0, \"shared_devices\": [], \"shared_ips\": []}\n\n        # Ego network up to specified radius\n        ego_nodes = nx.single_source_shortest_path_length(self.graph, txn_id, cutoff=depth)\n        subgraph = self.graph.subgraph(ego_nodes.keys())\n\n        nodes_out = []\n        for node_id in subgraph.nodes():\n            nd = dict(subgraph.nodes[node_id])\n            # Serialize sets\n            if \"accounts\" in nd:\n                nd[\"account_count\"] = len(nd[\"accounts\"])\n                nd[\"accounts\"] = list(nd[\"accounts\"])\n            nodes_out.append({\n                \"id\": str(node_id),\n                **nd\n            })\n\n        edges_out = []\n        for u, v, data in subgraph.edges(data=True):\n            edges_out.append({\n                \"source\": str(u),\n                \"target\": str(v),\n                \"relation\": data.get(\"relation\", \"CONNECTED\"),\n                \"evidence\": data.get(\"evidence\", \"Observed network link\")\n            })\n\n        # Identify shared entities in ego subgraph\n        shared_devices = [\n            n[\"id\"] for n in nodes_out\n            if n.get(\"node_type\") == \"device\" and n.get(\"account_count\", 0) > 1\n        ]\n        shared_ips = [\n            n[\"id\"] for n in nodes_out\n            if n.get(\"node_type\") == \"ip\" and n.get(\"account_count\", 0) > 1\n        ]\n\n        return {\n            \"root_transaction\": txn_id,\n            \"nodes\": nodes_out,\n            \"edges\": edges_out,\n            \"cluster_node_count\": len(nodes_out),\n            \"shared_devices\": shared_devices,\n            \"shared_ips\": shared_ips,\n            \"has_syndicate_overlap\": (len(shared_devices) > 0 or len(shared_ips) > 0)\n        }\n\n    def detect_syndicate_clusters(self, min_shared_accounts: int = 2) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Scans global graph for potential fraud syndicates:\n        Clusters where 2 or more distinct accounts share the same physical device or IP.\n        \"\"\"\n        syndicates = []\n        for dev_id, data in self.graph.nodes(data=True):\n            if data.get(\"node_type\") == \"device\":\n                accounts = list(data.get(\"accounts\", set()))\n                if len(accounts) >= min_shared_accounts:\n                    # Gather related transactions\n                    connected_txns = [\n                        neighbor for neighbor in self.graph.neighbors(dev_id)\n                        if self.graph.nodes[neighbor].get(\"node_type\") == \"transaction\"\n                    ]\n                    syndicates.append({\n                        \"entity_type\": \"device\",\n                        \"entity_id\": dev_id,\n                        \"shared_account_count\": len(accounts),\n                        \"accounts\": accounts,\n                        \"associated_transactions\": connected_txns,\n                        \"risk_level\": \"CRITICAL\" if len(accounts) >= 3 else \"HIGH\",\n                        \"narrative\": f\"Device {dev_id} shared across {len(accounts)} accounts ({', '.join(accounts[:3])}).\"\n                    })\n\n        return syndicates\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\backend\\app\\graph\\engine.py"}}]}
{"step_index":278,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:33:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T19:03:20+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T19:03:20+05:30\nCreated file."}
{"step_index":279,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T13:33:20Z","input_tokens":2506,"cache_read_tokens":105656,"output_tokens":3426,"thinking":"Considering the need for a database to store audit logs, investigator feedback, review decisions, and overrides, the initial plan involves using SQLite for local demonstrations. A repository abstraction will be implemented to facilitate a switch to PostgreSQL later. This structure supports recording case outcomes, including fraud confirmation, legitimate transactions, inconclusive results, and escalation for further review.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\"\"\nFraudLens AI - Database Layer & Repository Pattern\nSupports SQLite out of the box with clean abstract repository interface\nready to swap in PostgreSQL / SQLAlchemy for enterprise deployment.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sqlite3\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nDB_FILE = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / \"data\" / \"fraudlens.db\"\n\nclass DatabaseManager:\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = str(DB_FILE)):\n        self.db_path = db_path\n        self._init_db()\n\n    def get_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        conn = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path)\n        conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        return conn\n\n    def _init_db(self):\n        with self.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            # 1. Investigator Feedback & Audit History\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS investigator_feedback (\n                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    transaction_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    decision TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    reviewer_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    notes TEXT,\n                    model_version TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    original_model_score REAL,\n                    original_category TEXT,\n                    is_override INTEGER DEFAULT 0,\n                    created_at TEXT NOT NULL\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n\n            # 2. Scored Transactions Store (Local Fast Query & Filter Cache)\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS transactions (\n                    transaction_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n                    timestamp TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    account_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    amount REAL NOT NULL,\n                    currency TEXT DEFAULT 'USD',\n                    merchant_id TEXT,\n                    merchant_category TEXT,\n                    device_id TEXT,\n                    ip_address TEXT,\n                    location_country TEXT,\n                    account_age_days INTEGER,\n                    failed_attempts_last_24h INTEGER,\n                    is_fraud_label INTEGER,\n                    risk_score REAL,\n                    calibrated_prob REAL,\n                    triage_category TEXT,\n                    uncertainty_indicator REAL,\n                    review_priority REAL,\n                    model_version TEXT,\n                    investigation_status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending_review',\n                    assigned_investigator TEXT DEFAULT 'Unassigned',\n                    feature_contributions_json TEXT,\n                    raw_features_json TEXT\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n\n            # 3. System Audit Log\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS audit_log (\n                    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    event_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    details_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    timestamp TEXT NOT NULL\n                )\n            \"\"\")\n            conn.commit()\n\nclass FeedbackRepository:\n    def __init__(self, db_manager: DatabaseManager):\n        self.db = db_manager\n\n    def record_feedback(\n        self,\n        transaction_id: str,\n        decision: str,\n        reviewer_name: str,\n        notes: Optional[str],\n        model_version: str,\n        original_model_score: Optional[float],\n        original_category: Optional[str]\n    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        # Validate decision value\n        valid_decisions = [\"confirmed_fraud\", \"legitimate\", \"inconclusive\", \"escalated\"]\n        if decision not in valid_decisions:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid decision '{decision}'. Must be one of {valid_decisions}\")\n\n        # Check if this decision is an override\n        # e.g., Model said HIGH RISK, but investigator marked 'legitimate', or LOWER RISK marked 'confirmed_fraud'\n        is_override = 0\n        if original_category == \"HIGH RISK\" and decision == \"legitimate\":\n            is_override = 1\n        elif original_category == \"LOWER RISK\" and decision == \"confirmed_fraud\":\n            is_override = 1\n\n        now = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\n\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO investigator_feedback (\n                    transaction_id, decision, reviewer_name, notes,\n                    model_version, original_model_score, original_category,\n                    is_override, created_at\n                ) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n            \"\"\", (\n                transaction_id, decision, reviewer_name, notes or \"\",\n                model_version, original_model_score, original_category,\n                is_override, now\n            ))\n\n            # Update status in transactions table\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                UPDATE transactions\n                SET investigation_status = ?, assigned_investigator = ?\n                WHERE transaction_id = ?\n            \"\"\", (decision, reviewer_name, transaction_id))\n\n            # Add to audit log\n            audit_entry = {\n                \"transaction_id\": transaction_id,\n                \"action\": \"INVESTIGATOR_DECISION_RECORDED\",\n                \"decision\": decision,\n                \"reviewer\": reviewer_name,\n                \"is_override\": bool(is_override)\n            }\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                INSERT INTO audit_log (event_type, details_json, timestamp)\n                VALUES (?, ?, ?)\n            \"\"\", (\"FEEDBACK_SUBMITTED\", json.dumps(audit_entry), now))\n\n            conn.commit()\n            record_id = cursor.lastrowid\n\n        return {\n            \"id\": record_id,\n            \"transaction_id\": transaction_id,\n            \"decision\": decision,\n            \"reviewer_name\": reviewer_name,\n            \"notes\": notes,\n            \"is_override\": bool(is_override),\n            \"created_at\": now\n        }\n\n    def list_feedback(self, limit: int = 100) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                SELECT * FROM investigator_feedback\n                ORDER BY created_at DESC\n                LIMIT ?\n            \"\"\", (limit,))\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            return [dict(row) for row in rows]\n\nclass TransactionRepository:\n    def __init__(self, db_manager: DatabaseManager):\n        self.db = db_manager\n\n    def save_scored_transactions_batch(self, transactions: List[Dict[str, Any]]):\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            for t in transactions:\n                cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                    INSERT OR REPLACE INTO transactions (\n                        transaction_id, timestamp, account_id, amount, currency,\n                        merchant_id, merchant_category, device_id, ip_address,\n                        location_country, account_age_days, failed_attempts_last_24h,\n                        is_fraud_label, risk_score, calibrated_prob, triage_category,\n                        uncertainty_indicator, review_priority, model_version,\n                        investigation_status, assigned_investigator,\n                        feature_contributions_json, raw_features_json\n                    ) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n                \"\"\", (\n                    t[\"transaction_id\"], t[\"timestamp\"], t[\"account_id\"], t[\"amount\"], t.get(\"currency\", \"USD\"),\n                    t.get(\"merchant_id\"), t.get(\"merchant_category\"), t.get(\"device_id\"), t.get(\"ip_address\"),\n                    t.get(\"location_country\"), t.get(\"account_age_days\"), t.get(\"failed_attempts_last_24h\"),\n                    t.get(\"is_fraud\"), t.get(\"risk_score\"), t.get(\"calibrated_prob\"), t.get(\"triage_category\"),\n                    t.get(\"uncertainty_indicator\"), t.get(\"review_priority\"), t.get(\"model_version\"),\n                    t.get(\"investigation_status\", \"pending_review\"), t.get(\"assigned_investigator\", \"Unassigned\"),\n                    json.dumps(t.get(\"feature_contributions\", [])),\n                    json.dumps(t.get(\"raw_features\", {}))\n                ))\n            conn.commit()\n\n    def get_transaction_by_id(self, txn_id: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT * FROM transactions WHERE transaction_id = ?\", (txn_id,))\n            row = cursor.fetchone()\n            if not row:\n                return None\n            res = dict(row)\n            if res.get(\"feature_contributions_json\"):\n                res[\"feature_contributions\"] = json.loads(res[\"feature_contributions_json\"])\n            if res.get(\"raw_features_json\"):\n                res[\"raw_features\"] = json.loads(res[\"raw_features_json\"])\n            return res\n\n    def query_queue(\n        self,\n        triage_category: Optional[str] = None,\n        min_risk: Optional[float] = None,\n        status: Optional[str] = None,\n        sort_by: str = \"review_priority\",\n        ascending: bool = False,\n        limit: int = 150\n    ) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        query = \"SELECT * FROM transactions WHERE 1=1\"\n        params = []\n\n        if triage_category and triage_category != \"ALL\":\n            query += \" AND triage_category = ?\"\n            params.append(triage_category)\n        if min_risk is not None:\n            query += \" AND risk_score >= ?\"\n            params.append(min_risk)\n        if status and status != \"ALL\":\n            query += \" AND investigation_status = ?\"\n            params.append(status)\n\n        # Allowable sort columns\n        allowed_sorts = [\"review_priority\", \"risk_score\", \"uncertainty_indicator\", \"amount\", \"timestamp\"]\n        sort_col = sort_by if sort_by in allowed_sorts else \"review_priority\"\n        order = \"ASC\" if ascending else \"DESC\"\n        query += f\" ORDER BY {sort_col} {order} LIMIT ?\"\n        params.append(limit)\n\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(query, tuple(params))\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            results = []\n            for r in rows:\n                item = dict(r)\n                if item.get(\"feature_contributions_json\"):\n                    item[\"feature_contributions\"] = json.loads(item[\"feature_contributions_json\"])\n                results.append(item)\n            return results\n\n    def get_timeline_for_account(self, account_id: str) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"\"\"\n                SELECT * FROM transactions\n                WHERE account_id = ?\n                ORDER BY timestamp ASC\n            \"\"\", (account_id,))\n            rows = cursor.fetchall()\n            return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    def count_summary(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        with self.db.get_connection() as conn:\n            cursor = conn.cursor()\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM transactions\")\n            total = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM transactions WHERE triage_category = 'HIGH RISK'\")\n            high_risk = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM transactions WHERE triage_category = 'UNCERTAIN'\")\n            uncertain = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM transactions WHERE triage_category = 'LOWER RISK'\")\n            lower_risk = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM investigator_feedback WHERE decision = 'confirmed_fraud'\")\n            confirmed_fraud = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            cursor.execute(\"SELECT COUNT(*) FROM investigator_feedback WHERE is_override = 1\")\n            overrides = cursor.fetchone()[0]\n\n            return {\n                \"total_analyzed\": total,\n                \"high_risk_cases\": high_risk,\n                \"uncertain_cases\": uncertain,\n                \"lower_risk_cases\": lower_risk,\n                \"confirmed_fraud_feedback\": confirmed_fraud,\n                \"investigator_overrides\": overrides\n            }\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\S Nandhakumar\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\fraudlens-ai\\backend\\app\\db\\repository.py"}}]}
